{"blocks":[["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/02%20How%20It%20Works/03%20Vocoder%20Osc/","source-block-299","A carrier rich in overtones gives the vocoder more material to shape. Use the Wave knob to move through sawtooth, pulse width, and noise waves; see also Microfreak/UG/06 Dig Osc/03 Types/22 Vocoder.",["19.2.3. The Vocoder Oscillator"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/02%20How%20It%20Works/03%20Vocoder%20Osc/","source-block-509","The Digital Oscillator",["19.2.3. The Vocoder Oscillator"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/02%20How%20It%20Works/03%20Vocoder%20Osc/","source-block-760","Wave positions",["19.2.3. The Vocoder Oscillator"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/02%20How%20It%20Works/03%20Vocoder%20Osc/","source-block-778","0%: sawtooth.",["19.2.3. The Vocoder Oscillator","Wave positions"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/02%20How%20It%20Works/03%20Vocoder%20Osc/","source-block-796","Around 11%: pulse wave at 50% duty cycle.",["19.2.3. The Vocoder Oscillator","Wave positions"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/02%20How%20It%20Works/03%20Vocoder%20Osc/","source-block-842","From 11% to 90%: increasing pulse width, reaching 97% duty cycle.",["19.2.3. The Vocoder Oscillator","Wave positions"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/02%20How%20It%20Works/03%20Vocoder%20Osc/","source-block-912","91–100%: noise.",["19.2.3. The Vocoder Oscillator","Wave positions"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/02%20How%20It%20Works/03%20Vocoder%20Osc/","source-block-1075","Sawtooth, pulse-width, and noise waveforms",["19.2.3. The Vocoder Oscillator"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/02%20How%20It%20Works/03%20Vocoder%20Osc/","source-block-1336","Timbre and Shape also control the Vocoder Oscillator.",["19.2.3. The Vocoder Oscillator"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/02%20How%20It%20Works/03%20Vocoder%20Osc/01%20Timbre/","source-block-232","19.2.3.1. Timbre Encoder",[]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/02%20How%20It%20Works/03%20Vocoder%20Osc/01%20Timbre/","source-block-261","Timbre selects the frequency range used for analysis and resynthesis. Vowel formants peak at different frequencies: for example, a “u” may have peaks near 330 and 1260 Hz, with variation across voices.",["19.2.3.1. Timbre Encoder"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/02%20How%20It%20Works/03%20Vocoder%20Osc/01%20Timbre/","source-block-474","Matching the range to the speaker, or to an instrument used as a modulator, helps the filters respond to the frequencies that matter. Monitoring fewer frequencies can improve response time and output.",["19.2.3.1. Timbre Encoder"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/02%20How%20It%20Works/03%20Vocoder%20Osc/01%20Timbre/","source-block-678","Vocoder filter bands and frequency response",["19.2.3.1. Timbre Encoder"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/02%20How%20It%20Works/03%20Vocoder%20Osc/01%20Timbre/Asset/01-Vocoder-filter-bands/png/","source-block-57","01 Vocoder filter bands",[]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/02%20How%20It%20Works/03%20Vocoder%20Osc/02%20Shape/","source-block-295","19.2.3.2. Shape Encoder",[]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/02%20How%20It%20Works/03%20Vocoder%20Osc/02%20Shape/","source-block-323","Shape sets the bandwidth of each bandpass filter. Higher settings narrow the filters' frequency response and produce more pronounced harmonics.",["19.2.3.2. Shape Encoder"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/02%20How%20It%20Works/03%20Vocoder%20Osc/Asset/01-The-Digital-Oscillator/png/","source-block-57","01 The Digital Oscillator",[]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/02%20How%20It%20Works/03%20Vocoder%20Osc/Asset/02-Vocoder-waveforms/png/","source-block-57","02 Vocoder waveforms",[]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/02%20How%20It%20Works/Asset/01-Vocoder-signal-path/png/","source-block-57","01 Vocoder signal path",[]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/03%20Connect%20Mic/","source-block-239","19.3. Connect the Microphone",[]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/03%20Connect%20Mic/","source-block-272","Insert the microphone unit into the headphone input. Align the black plastic gooseneck adapter with the edges of the MicroFreak case and press gently but firmly. To monitor with headphones, plug them into the output at the microphone base.",["19.3. Connect the Microphone"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/04%20Headset%20Mic/","source-block-241","19.4. (Or) Connect a Headset Microphone",[]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/04%20Headset%20Mic/","source-block-285","Insert the headset microphone's 3.5 mm TRRS plug into the MicroFreak headphone jack.",["19.4. (Or) Connect a Headset Microphone"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/05%20Vocoder%20Preset/","source-block-238","19.5. Select a Vocoder Preset",[]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/05%20Vocoder%20Preset/","source-block-272","The MicroFreak Vocoder Limited Edition includes vocoder presets in memory locations 304–320. Turn the Preset knob to select one. A three-step VU meter appears when a vocoder preset is loaded and responds to your voice level.",["19.5. Select a Vocoder Preset"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/05%20Vocoder%20Preset/","source-block-502","To start from an INIT preset, turn the Digital Oscillator Type knob clockwise and select Vocoder.",["19.5. Select a Vocoder Preset"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/05%20Vocoder%20Preset/","source-block-611","To save the preset:",["19.5. Select a Vocoder Preset"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/05%20Vocoder%20Preset/","source-block-634","Click the encoder.",["19.5. Select a Vocoder Preset","To save the preset:"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/05%20Vocoder%20Preset/","source-block-657","Turn it to select the vocoder category.",["19.5. Select a Vocoder Preset","To save the preset:"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/05%20Vocoder%20Preset/","source-block-701","Click it again and optionally name the preset.",["19.5. Select a Vocoder Preset","To save the preset:"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/05%20Vocoder%20Preset/","source-block-752","Click Save.",["19.5. Select a Vocoder Preset","To save the preset:"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/06%20Play%20%26%20Sing/","source-block-236","19.6. Play & Sing",[]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/06%20Play%20%26%20Sing/","source-block-258","Press a key while speaking or singing into the microphone to hear your voice resynthesized by the Vocoder Oscillator. The keyboard determines the output pitch; the vocoder follows the volume and timbre of your voice, not the notes you sing.",["19.6. Play & Sing"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/06%20Play%20%26%20Sing/","source-block-502","While playing, adjust the Digital Oscillator's Wave, Timbre, and Shape controls. Turn on Paraphonic mode to vocode chords by playing two or more keys while singing.",["19.6. Play & Sing"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/07%20Config/","source-block-242","19.7. Vocoder Configuration",[]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/07%20Config/","source-block-274","The Vocoder settings can be adjusted as the voice or microphone changes. Global Utility settings affect every vocoder preset; settings under Utility > Preset are saved with the current preset.",["19.7. Vocoder Configuration"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/07%20Config/","source-block-474","The global settings can be changed on the MicroFreak or in the MIDI Control Center.",["19.7. Vocoder Configuration"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/07%20Config/","source-block-561","Mic Settings",["19.7. Vocoder Configuration"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/07%20Config/","source-block-580","Mic Gain: -12 dB to +59 dB, or Auto Gain (default).",["19.7. Vocoder Configuration","Mic Settings"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/07%20Config/","source-block-640","Noise Gate: Off or a threshold; default -70 dB.",["19.7. Vocoder Configuration","Mic Settings"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/07%20Config/","source-block-696","Mic Detection: Off or On (default).",["19.7. Vocoder Configuration","Mic Settings"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/07%20Config/01%20Preset%20Settings/","source-block-190","19.7.1. Preset related Vocoder settings",[]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/07%20Config/01%20Preset%20Settings/","source-block-234","Two settings under Utility > Preset are saved with each preset:",["19.7.1. Preset related Vocoder settings"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/07%20Config/01%20Preset%20Settings/","source-block-305","Vocoder Hiss Mode",["19.7.1. Preset related Vocoder settings","Two settings under Utility > Preset are saved with each preset:"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/07%20Config/01%20Preset%20Settings/","source-block-331","Vocoder Hiss Vol",["19.7.1. Preset related Vocoder settings","Two settings under Utility > Preset are saved with each preset:"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/07%20Config/01%20Preset%20Settings/","source-block-356","Older vocoders added high-frequency noise (“hiss”) to the lower, voiced “buzz” range to make consonants easier to understand.",["19.7.1. Preset related Vocoder settings"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/07%20Config/01%20Preset%20Settings/","source-block-493","Vocoder Hiss Mode",["19.7.1. Preset related Vocoder settings"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/07%20Config/01%20Preset%20Settings/","source-block-517","Off: Only the lower, vowel-like buzz range is heard.",["19.7.1. Preset related Vocoder settings","Vocoder Hiss Mode"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/07%20Config/01%20Preset%20Settings/","source-block-578","Switched: A detector distinguishes voiced sections from unvoiced sections. During an unvoiced section, white noise replaces the carrier oscillator. Output is gated by the modulator and follows its level.",["19.7.1. Preset related Vocoder settings","Vocoder Hiss Mode"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/07%20Config/01%20Preset%20Settings/","source-block-790","Pass: The vocoded synth signal is mixed with the part of the microphone signal above 5 kHz, allowing the high frequencies of the voice through.",["19.7.1. Preset related Vocoder settings","Vocoder Hiss Mode"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/07%20Config/01%20Preset%20Settings/","source-block-942","Vocoder Hiss Vol",["19.7.1. Preset related Vocoder settings"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/07%20Config/01%20Preset%20Settings/","source-block-965","Sets the level of hiss mixed with the microphone signal and the white-noise replacement level in Switched mode, from -20 dB to 0 dB.",["19.7.1. Preset related Vocoder settings","Vocoder Hiss Vol"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/","source-block-229","19.8. Global Vocoder settings",[]]],"format_version":5}